	(text "Isolation: with JP1 and JP2 open the stove side (GND_S, +5V_S, DATA_S, +20V_S) is galvanically separated;\nthe optocouplers are powered from the stove's 5 V. Closing JP1 + JP2 powers the board from the stove's 20 V,\nwhich connects GND_S to GND (USB / PC ground) - only when the stove's low voltage is safely isolated from mains.\nThe echo of our own TX on RX is kept on purpose: the firmware uses it to tell a missing bus from a silent stove."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 266.7 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "101e02fc-394c-5005-8dfa-51c00ade55ab")
	)
	(text "GPIO: IO17 STOVE_TX (UART1), IO18 STOVE_RX, IO8 LED data, IO0 BOOT / user button,\nIO21 buzzer, IO4 power source (high = stove), IO19/20 USB D-/D+. Strapping pins IO3, IO45, IO46 unconnected (defaults).\nD5 shows the serial line in hardware: red = TX, green = RX (orange while sending: echo).\nDraft for review before ordering."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 304.8 248.92 0)
		(effects
